    "notes": "The centrepiece: ONE local_id (wallet-btc:txid_reorg_1) goes active(pending) -> TOMBSTONED(reorged_out) -> active(posted), one observation per page, and expect.ledger declares all three IN THAT ORDER. Tombstone is NOT terminal. The whole chain is the assertion: an adapter that drops the middle page reports active then active, the vanish never happened, and its final live set is byte-identical to the correct one -- only sequence equality over the full retained history (A8, enforced inside A2) can contradict it. Emitting the three in the wrong order (tombstone last) is likewise a different sequence and likewise fails. The local_id is the SAME throughout, unlike pending_to_posted.json where posting forks identity: bank pending->posted forks, bitcoin re-mining does not, and one fold must handle both. expect.live is DECLARED as the single surviving id, not derived by folding the sequence above."
